# Gitignored files Claude Code copies into every new worktree it creates.
# `.gitignore` syntax; only files that match *and* are gitignored are copied,
# so nothing tracked is ever duplicated.
#
# The dev database is here because a worktree is a fresh checkout and `/.data`
# is ignored, so without this every worktree starts with zero accounts — and
# a login screen with no account behind it fails ten times and then throttles
# for fifteen minutes. See docs/TESTING.md.
#
# `-wal` is not optional. SQLite in WAL mode leaves most recent writes in the
# sidecar, so copying `kilorep.db` alone hands the worktree a stale database
# that is missing whatever the last session did. `-shm` is deliberately absent:
# it is a shared-memory index tied to the process that held it, and SQLite
# rebuilds it on open.
.data/kilorep.db
.data/kilorep.db-wal

# `.env` is not present yet — the defaults in `src/lib/server/env.ts` carry local
# dev on their own. Listed anyway so the day one appears, it stops being the thing
# that works in the main checkout and nowhere else. `.env.dev` is the same argument
# and does exist: without it a worktree's `bun run dev` has no Google client, and
# the login screen answers that by drawing no button and explaining nothing.
.env
.env.dev
